  "name": "Uncanny Dodge (Ex)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "subType": "classFeat",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Starting at 4th level, a thief can react to danger before her senses would normally allow her to do so. She cannot be caught flat-footed, nor does she lose her Dexterity bonus to AC if the attacker is invisible. She still loses her Dexterity bonus to AC if immobilized. A thief with this ability can still lose her Dexterity bonus to AC if an opponent successfully uses the feint action against her. If a thief already has uncanny dodge from a different class, she automatically gains improved uncanny dodge (see below) instead.</p>",
